cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this work, cite it with the metadata below. This describes a
  release-readiness candidate of an AI-assisted, independently audited Lean 4
  formalization; it is not a published release and no human semantic review
  of the proofs has taken place. See docs/RELEASE_READINESS.md.
type: software
title: >-
  formal-science: a machine-checked two-state Lindblad benchmark and finite
  Markov generator bridge in Lean 4 and Mathlib
authors:
  - family-names: Sturges
    given-names: Jett
version: 0.0.1
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/jsturges28/materials-qc-formalization
abstract: >-
  Eight Lean 4 release modules over pinned Mathlib: qubit density states and
  finite Kraus sums, the finite dissipator algebra, the two-state stationary
  state and its uniqueness, the explicit two-state evolution with semigroup
  and derivative laws, its four-Kraus certification with all-finite-ancilla
  complete positivity, quantitative Frobenius convergence to the stationary
  projection, and a zero-Hamiltonian finite Markov generator bridge. Every
  export depends only on propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - open quantum systems
  - Lindblad equation
  - Kraus representation
  - Markov generator
